  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You choose up to four nonmagical sticks no longer than a Quarterstaff (or similar pieces of nonmagical wood, such as Torches or Spears) that you can see within range, and they shape-shift into snakes. A creature holding a targeted object can make a Charisma saving throw; on a success, that object doesn’t shape-shift. Each shape-shifted object uses the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.actors24.Actor.mmVenomousSnake0]{Venomous Snake} stat block.</p><p>Each snake is Friendly to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count and takes its turn immediately after yours.</p><p>Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature made by this spell that is within 500 feet of you (if you control several, you can command any of them at the same time, giving each the same command). If you give no commands, a snake takes the Dodge action and moves only to avoid harm. When a snake drops to 0 Hit Points, it returns to its object form, and any remaining damage carries over to that form.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> You can target two additional objects for each spell slot level above 4.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-cuN23JR5zY7z4hao\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon places the snakes; remove the sticks from the scene by hand.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
